To find the remainder of $2^{2005}$ when divided by 7, we can use the concept of modular arithmetic. We can express $2^{2005}$ as $(2^3)^668 \times 2$.
answer: Now \begin{align*}2^3&=8\equiv1\pmod 7\\ \implies(2^3)^668&\equiv 1^{668}\pmod 7\\ &=1\pmod 7\\ \implies \color{red}{2^{2005}}&\equiv\color{green}{2\times1}\equiv\color{blue}2\pmod 7\end{align*}
